{
  "id": "calcium_silicate_insulation",
  "title": "Calcium Silicate Insulation",
  "description": "Thermal conductivity calculator for calcium silicate insulation - analyze k-values across temperature ranges from 250°F (121°C) to 1000°F (540°C)",
  "type": "calculator-chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Calcium Silicate Insulation\n\nCalcium silicate is a rigid, high-density material used as a safe alternative to asbestos for high-temperature insulation applications.\n\n### Key Features:\n- Light weight\n- Low thermal conductivity\n- High temperature and chemical resistance\n- Noncombustible\n- Good compressive strength\n\n### Application Range:\n250°F (121°C) to 1000°F (540°C)\n\n### Conversion Factors:\n- Temperature: T(°C) = 5/9 × (T(°F) - 32)\n- Thermal Conductivity: 1 W/(m·K) = 6.935 Btu·in/(h·ft²·°F)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "temperature_f",
          "label": "Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 400,
          "unit": "°F"
        },
        {
          "id": "unit_system",
          "label": "Unit System",
          "type": "select",
          "defaultValue": "metric",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Metric (W/m·K)",
              "value": "metric"
            },
            {
              "label": "Imperial (Btu·in/h·ft²·°F)",
              "value": "imperial"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "temperature_c",
          "label": "Temperature (Celsius)",
          "formula": "(inputs.temperature_f - 32) * 5 / 9",
          "unit": "°C",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "k_value_metric",
          "label": "Thermal Conductivity (Metric)",
          "formula": "0.05 + 0.00012 * inputs.temperature_f",
          "unit": "W/(m·K)",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "k_value_imperial",
          "label": "Thermal Conductivity (Imperial)",
          "formula": "(0.05 + 0.00012 * inputs.temperature_f) * 6.935",
          "unit": "Btu·in/(h·ft²·°F)",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
